{
  "id": "COMPOUND:26074 - PROTEIN:5864",
  "verbalization": "Epi-Fibrauretinoside A is implicated in the biological activity of U373 MG cells through a multi-step pathway involving dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases. This kinase is targeted by 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine and also by Corticatic Acid E, both of which are known to interact with U373 MG. The evidence suggests that Epi-Fibrauretinoside A acts as a regulator of the kinase pathway, which in turn influences the behavior of U373 MG cells. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway, including a structurally distinct compound, indicates that Epi-Fibrauretinoside A may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the modulation of kinase activity, potentially through direct interaction or by influencing the expression or function of the kinase. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the signaling network in U373 MG cells and underscores the role of kinase regulation in cellular response to Epi-Fibrauretinoside A.",
